.TH buffer_dump 3
.SH NAME
buffer_dump \- print a representation of buffer state to an output buffer
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include "buffer.h"

void buffer_dump(buffer* \fIout\fP, buffer* \fIb\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B buffer_dump
formats the current state of the buffer structure
.I b
into a human-readable string and writes it to the output buffer
.I out\fP.

The output includes:
.IP \(bu 2
.B p:
The current buffer position (offset).
.IP \(bu 2
.B n:
The number of bytes currently stored in the buffer.
.IP \(bu 2
.B a:
The total allocated size of the buffer.
.IP \(bu 2
.B fd:
The file descriptor associated with the buffer.
.IP \(bu 2
.B op:
The function pointer used for I/O operations (represented as a descriptive label
or memory address if unrecognized).

If the project is compiled with COLOR_DUMP, the output is formatted with ANSI
escape sequences for better visibility in terminal environments.
.SH SEE ALSO
buffer_puts(3), buffer_putnlflush(3)